  {
   "id": 669011,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" type=\"1\">\n  <li>A store receives 2,000 decks of popular trading cards. The number of decks of cards is a function, <span data-math=\"d\">d</span>, of the number of days, <span data-math=\"t\">t</span><em>,</em> since the shipment arrived. Here is a table showing some values of <span data-math=\"d\">d</span><em>.</em><br> <br>     <table class=\"unnumbered\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"t\">t</span></th>\n          <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"d(t)\">d(t)</span></th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr>\n          <td>0</td>\n          <td>2,000</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>5</td>\n          <td>1,283</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>10</td>\n          <td>823</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>15</td>\n          <td>528</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td>20</td>\n          <td>338</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n <br> Calculate the average rate of change for the following intervals: <br> <br></li>\n  </ol><ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"1\" type=\"a\">\n    <li>day 0 to day 5</li>\n  </ol>",
